{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterGeometricRepresentationFull","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterRankTwo"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.bond_ne_zero_of_pow_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.bond_ne_zero_of_pow_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L316-L325","doc":"**A trivial positive power of `σᵢσⱼ` forces the bond order to be finite.**\n\nThe companion of `dihedralExact_full` at the other end of the range, and the input that lets the\ndescent lemma *derive* `M i j ≠ 0` instead of assuming it: at `M i j = 0` the rotation `fᵢfⱼ` is a\nshear of infinite order (`reflEnd_pair_pow_ne_one_of_infinite`), so no positive power of `σᵢσⱼ`\ncan be trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.dihedralExact_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.dihedralExact_full","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L306-L314","doc":"**`σᵢσⱼ` has order exactly `M i j`, in every Coxeter system.**\n\nThis is the second half of what `CoxeterGeometricRepresentationFull`'s HONESTY note excludes from\nits own scope, and it discharges `CoxeterRankTwo.DihedralExact` unconditionally — so Matsumoto,\nthe `T_w` basis, the subword property, Bruhat transitivity, lifting and the order equivalences hold\nfor every Coxeter system, not only type `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.reflEnd_pair_pow_ne_one_of_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.reflEnd_pair_pow_ne_one_of_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L282-L291","doc":"**At an infinite bond, `fᵢfⱼ` has infinite order.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.orbit_coeff_of_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.orbit_coeff_of_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L267-L280","doc":"**The `αᵢ`-coefficient along the orbit is `1 + 2k`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.orbit_succ_of_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.orbit_succ_of_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L250-L265","doc":"**The shear.** At an infinite bond, one step adds `2αᵢ + 2αⱼ` to the orbit vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_ySeq_of_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_ySeq_of_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L235-L248","doc":"At an infinite bond the scalar pair is constant, hence blind. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.reflEnd_pair_pow_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.reflEnd_pair_pow_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L174-L201","doc":"**No smaller positive power of `fᵢfⱼ` is the identity.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_eq_cos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_eq_cos","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L141-L170","doc":"**`⟨αᵢ, (fᵢfⱼ)^k αᵢ⟩ = cos (k · 2π/m)`.**\n\nThe whole content is that the initial data matches: `x 0 = 1 = cos 0` and, because\n`c = −cos(π/m)`, `x 1 = 2c² − 1 = 2cos²(π/m) − 1 = cos(2π/m)` by the double-angle formula. No\nsine, no invertibility, and `m ≥ 2` rather than `m ≥ 3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_one","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L133-L137","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.ySeq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.ySeq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L127-L131","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L121-L125","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_two_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_two_step","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L108-L117","doc":"**The Chebyshev recursion.** Eliminating `ySeq` between the two first-order relations leaves a\nsingle two-step recursion with `T = 4c² − 2`, which is `2 cos φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.ySeq_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.ySeq_succ","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L100-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq_succ","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L94-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.ySeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.ySeq","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L90-L92","doc":"`ySeq i j k = ⟨αⱼ, (fᵢfⱼ)^k αᵢ⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterDihedralOrder.xSeq","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterDihedralOrder.lean#L85-L87","doc":"`xSeq i j k = ⟨αᵢ, (fᵢfⱼ)^k αᵢ⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}